Found while measuring karr #138 (docs/adr/0042), not fixed there: lastmodified is the AAD of the metadata MAC, and sops does NOT use the documents literal text for it. It decodes the field into a Go time.Time and re-formats it as RFC3339 (Z), so a document spelling the same instant differently still verifies THERE and fails HERE.

MEASURED, sops 3.13.3, on a document sops itself wrote (only the lastmodified line edited):

  lastmodified: "2026-08-21T08:03:09Z"      sops -d exit 0   File::SOPS ok
  lastmodified: "2026-08-21T08:03:09+00:00" sops -d exit 0   File::SOPS DIES
        "Cannot decrypt MAC - refusing to return unverified data"
  lastmodified: 2026-08-21T08:03:09Z        sops -d exit 1   File::SOPS accepts
        (unquoted: go-yaml v3 resolves it as !!timestamp -> a time.Time where
         mapstructure wants a string, "decoding failed")
  lastmodified: "2026-08-21t08:03:09z"      sops -d exit 1   (parse error)
  lastmodified: "2026-08-21 08:03:09Z"      sops -d exit 1   (parse error)
  lastmodified: 2 / ""                      sops -d exit 1   (parse error)

So there are TWO divergences in opposite directions:
  1. A valid RFC3339 spelling that is not the canonical Z form: sops reads the file, we refuse it. Any offset form, and presumably a fractional-second one.
  2. An UNQUOTED timestamp: sops refuses the document, we accept it.

Both are AAD bytes, so this is the wire lane and not the api lane - Metadata.pm holds the attribute, but what bytes reach the AAD is Encrypted/the MAC path. Needs its own measurement of the full RFC3339 spelling set before anything is written.

Lane: wire.
MEASURED AND FIXED, direction 1. docs/adr/0044.

THE AAD PROOF, direct rather than inferred: documents whose lastmodified TEXT is one thing and whose mac was encrypted under a CHOSEN AAD, handed to sops -d.

  text "...09:05:08+00:00"  mac under "...09:05:08Z"       exit 0
  text "...09:05:08+00:00"  mac under the literal text     exit 51
  text "...09:05:08.123Z"   mac under "...09:05:08Z"       exit 0
  text "...09:05:08.123Z"   mac under the literal text     exit 51
  text "...11:05:08+02:00"  mac under the UTC form         exit 51
  text "...11:05:08+02:00"  mac under "...11:05:08+02:00"  exit 0

So the AAD is time.Parse(RFC3339,s).Format(RFC3339) and the ticket's premise is confirmed - with one correction the ticket did not have: a NON-ZERO offset is KEPT, not normalised to UTC. Only a ZERO offset becomes Z.

45 spellings measured. The round trip is purely lexical: fraction dropped (any length, comma as well as period), hour zero-padded (Go's 15 takes one digit or two where its 01/02/04/05 do not), zone re-derived from the TOTAL offset (+00:60 -> +01:00, +24:60 -> +25:00) and written Z whenever that total is zero. Offset hour 0..24 and minute 0..60 are in range; 25 and 61 are refused. No calendar arithmetic is involved.

FIXED in File::SOPS::Metadata->from_hash (ADR 0042's position, and the only one reachable without touching the two AAD call sites in SOPS.pm). 14 of 26 self-consistent spellings that sops -d reads at exit 0 used to die here with "Cannot decrypt MAC"; 0 do now. A spelling Go cannot parse is passed through unchanged rather than refused - karr #145's reasoning, one field over.

NOTHING MOVES for a document either implementation writes: nine-document corpus (4 by sops -e incl. --mac-only-encrypted and --unencrypted-suffix, 1 by --encrypted-suffix, 4 by File::SOPS->encrypt incl. json and mac_only_encrypted), AAD + decrypted MAC plaintext + decrypted values byte-identical before and after in all nine.

WRITE PATH CHECKED: File::SOPS::encrypt is the only producer, policy_args does not carry lastmodified, update_lastmodified is strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', gmtime). We have never written a spelling this moves.

DIRECTION 2 (unquoted timestamp) IS NOT FIXED HERE and is karr #159: from_hash sees the same Perl string for a bare and a quoted scalar (ADR 0038 measured that), so it cannot be implemented in Metadata.pm. Permissive, recorded, pinned in the new test.

